  m= 128: FAIL at d=69 (d/m=0.539)
  m= 256: FAIL at d=133 (d/m=0.520)
  m= 512: FAIL at d=263 (d/m=0.514)

4.2  the rescue: shell 128 absorbs shell 64's deficit at the SAME absolute degree d=36:
  shell 64:  demand has 59 bits, supply 59 bits -> deficit 55 bits
  shell 128: demand has 106 bits, supply 143 bits -> slack  143 bits
  two-shell tail cut at (M=64, d=36): SATISFIED (slack exceeds deficit by ~2^88)

4.3  ALL degree-resolved tail cuts over the window, exact:
  violated tail cuts: 819 total; of these, 819 have d > 255, where ONLY the deepest shell (m=512) has any demand or supply
  violated tail cuts with genuine multi-shell content (d <= 255): 0
  violated degrees: d in [263, 379]  (deepest shell's binding band, d/512 ~ 0.514..0.740)

  => every violated cut lives at degrees only the deepest shell reaches: the
     'binding degree-resolved cut' of THM-3024 (G3) is the deepest shell's OWN
     per-shell (ARCH) constraint -- a TRUNCATION EDGE ARTIFACT, not a cross-shell
     obstruction.  Any per-shell deficit interior to the window is absorbed by
     the next shell with exponential room (4.2).  In the model AS STATED
     (unbounded forward routing at fixed absolute degree), demand at fixed d
     grows polynomially in m while supply grows exponentially, so EVERY tail
     cut with an unbounded (or merely one-shell-deeper) tail is satisfied for
     ANY gamma > 0: the transportation relaxation yields NO general-class floor.

